{
 "result": "csvsum.py is done. It flattens the whole CSV into one token stream (CR removed, newlines turned into commas, split on commas), drops the 'id,cat,val' header, and sums val per cat with a dict over stride-3 zipped slices. It prints 'cat,sum' lines sorted by cat with 2 decimals. It passes the public sample (in-0 matches out-0). The assay registered a baseline of 2.00046 (noise 5%), and the flattened variant was adopted with a measured +6% gain over the earlier per-line version. I stopped here because further gains would need to beat the 5% noise band, and I did not find a clear candidate for that.",
